1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,384
Image models can now draw beautiful charts.

2
00:00:03,384 --> 00:00:06,810
But one wrong number, and the chart is useless.

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:14,320
In testing, Hy Image printed a world total of 23,000 as 28,000.

4
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:16,205
So we built Plate.

5
00:00:16,205 --> 00:00:23,030
It designs with Muse Spark, renders with Hy Image, and checks every label before you see it.

6
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:27,125
You paste your data, and pick a format and a style.

7
00:00:27,125 --> 00:00:27,820
That's it.

8
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:33,361
Muse Spark writes a spec with every word and number locked.

9
00:00:33,361 --> 00:00:35,468
Plate compiles the prompt.

10
00:00:35,468 --> 00:00:38,628
Hy Image renders it at 2K on GMI Cloud.

11
00:00:38,628 --> 00:00:41,221
Muse Spark reads it back, blind.

12
00:00:41,221 --> 00:00:46,326
Plate's code diffs every label, and Hy fixes only the mistakes.

13
00:00:46,326 --> 00:00:47,460
Then it loops.

14
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:48,816
Why blind?

15
00:00:48,816 --> 00:00:54,299
A reader who knows the answer tends to see it, even when it's wrong.

16
00:00:54,299 --> 00:00:58,330
So Muse Spark only reads, and Plate's code judges.

17
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:01,120
Here's a real run, sped up.

18
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:07,020
Plate's check caught Hy tying a note about the whole chart to Zambia.

19
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:10,932
One targeted Hy edit erased just that line.

20
00:01:10,932 --> 00:01:14,450
Everything else stayed exactly as Hy drew it.

21
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,920
You get the finished graphic, with takeaways, a caption, alt text and the data table.

22
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,080
Plate catches misspellings,

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,560
and numbers nobody asked for.

24
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:34,750
Plate does the heavy lifting, and it remembers what Hy gets wrong, so every render starts smarter.

25
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:41,770
Copper: Chile mined more than the United States, China and Russia combined.

26
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:47,120
Coffee: Brazil grows more than the next four countries together.

27
00:01:47,670 --> 00:01:52,630
Cotton: China grew more than Brazil and the United States combined.

28
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:58,700
Lithium: three countries mined nearly three-quarters, outside the U.S.

29
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:06,050
Material Facts: every chart built from what it measures, and every label checked by Plate.

30
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:07,108
Plate.

31
00:02:07,108 --> 00:02:08,631
Hy Image draws it.

32
00:02:08,631 --> 00:02:10,000
Plate makes sure it's right.
